Steam Enhanced, core/runtime.js: SE.poll checks run at the start of a frame.

Why. SE.poll's timer calls `active` first, and most polls answer it with SE.visible() →
checkVisibility(), which needs up-to-date styles. From a timer task, while the page is changing,
that forces a style recalculation of the whole window on top of the one the next frame does
anyway (up to ~145 ms in the main window). Measured on one game page change (570 → 730):
checkVisibility via hasBox/visible 171 ms of forced style work, called from the polls of
client/game-page/player-count.js, downloads, the friends list and collections.

What. The poll's timer no longer calls tick() itself: it asks for the next animation frame
(tickInFrame), and tick() runs there, where the style pass is the frame's own. One frame request
at a time; disconnect() cancels it; a window without requestAnimationFrame ticks at once as
before. Hidden documents: the frame comes when the document is shown, and tick() checks the
visibility first as before. wake() (resize, focus) is unchanged.

--- a/core/runtime.js
+++ b/core/runtime.js
